@node Top
@top CPF and CNPJ Tools

This manual documents @code{cpf-tools}, an Emacs package for generating, validating, and formatting Brazilian CPF and CNPJ numbers.

@menu
* Overview::             What cpf-tools does.
* Installation::         How to install the package.
* Usage::                Commands and functions reference.
@end menu

@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@code{cpf-tools} provides utilities for working with Brazilian personal (CPF) and corporate (CNPJ) tax identification numbers. Features include:
@itemize
@item Generating valid CPF and CNPJ numbers (with prefix arguments for insertion or formatting).
@item Validating CPF and CNPJ numbers.
@item Formatting text regions containing CPF or CNPJ numbers.
@item Completing incomplete CPF and CNPJ patterns containing wildcards (@code{*} or @code{?}).
@end itemize

@node Installation
@chapter Installation

You can install @code{cpf-tools} from MELPA or directly from source:

@itemize
@item Using @code{use-package} and @code{:vc}:
@example
(use-package cpf-tools
  :ensure t
  :vc (:url "https://github.com/jjnilton/cpf-tools" :rev :newest))
@end example
@item Using @code{package-install-file}:
@example
M-x package-install-file RET cpf-tools.el RET
@end example
@end itemize

@node Usage
@chapter Usage

Here are the primary interactive commands and functions provided by @code{cpf-tools}:

@table @code
@item cpf-tools-generate-cpf (&optional arg)
Generate a valid CPF number. Prefix arguments control output and insertion:
@itemize
@item @code{nil}: Output unformatted to @code{*Messages*}.
@item @code{C-u}: Insert unformatted at point.
@item @code{C-u C-u}: Output formatted to @code{*Messages*}.
@item @code{C-u C-u C-u}: Insert formatted at point.
@end itemize

@item cpf-tools-generate-cnpj (&optional arg)
Generate a valid CNPJ number (supports the same prefix arguments as @code{generate-cpf}).

@item cpf-tools-complete-cpf (incomplete-cpf-string)
Find and display valid CPF numbers matching an incomplete pattern with wildcards (@code{*} or @code{?}), such as @code{***.781.235-**}.

@item cpf-tools-complete-cnpj (incomplete-cnpj-string)
Find and display valid CNPJ numbers matching an incomplete pattern with wildcards (@code{*} or @code{?}).

@item cpf-tools-format-cpf-region (beg end)
Format the marked region as CPF.

@item cpf-tools-format-cnpj-region (beg end)
Format the marked region as CNPJ.

@item cpf-tools-format-cpf-cnpj-region (beg end)
Format the marked region as CPF or CNPJ automatically based on its length.
@end table

@bye
